  "notes": "{焦|じ}らす means to deliberately make someone wait or withhold something, causing impatience or frustration.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {焦|じ}れる (intransitive — to grow impatient)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{焦|じ}らしている means \"is keeping someone in suspense\" (ongoing action).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {相手|あいて}を{焦|じ}らす: to keep someone in suspense\n- {焦|じ}らさないで: don't keep me waiting/don't tease me\n- じらしプレー: playing hard to get, teasing play\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {焦|じ}れる: to grow impatient (intransitive)\n- {焦|あせ}る: to be in a hurry, to feel anxious/impatient\n- じれったい: frustrating, exasperating (adjective)",
